B.a3b=new A.jg("Receipt subtotal and main category",B.KQ,null)
B.a2R=new A.dA('For anything that is not the main category, type a few letters of its category and press Enter: "to" for Toiletries. The category\'s name appears beside the letters once they match exactly one.',null)
B.a2J=new A.dA("The cursor moves to Items. Type how many lines of the receipt are in that category and press Enter: that many boxes appear, Item 1, Item 2 and so on. Type each price before tax and press Enter to move to the next. Their total shows underneath.",null)
B.a2z=new A.dA("Rebates and instant savings, like Costco's, are lines of their own on the receipt, so count them as items and type them with a minus: -3.00. If you counted one short, Add item makes another box.",null)
B.a2w=new A.dA("After the last item, the cursor goes to the letters for the next category. Press Enter there with no letters when you have no more, and you are on to the note. Backspace on empty letters removes that category.",null)
B.a2N=new A.dA("The main category gets the rest of the subtotal automatically, so you never add anything up. A rebate on a main-category item needs nothing typed, because the subtotal already includes it.",null)
B.a2H=new A.dA('Letters only pick a category when exactly one name starts with them. If they could mean two, like "g" for Gas or Groceries, it says so and waits for another letter. Typing the whole name always works. The shortest letters for your usual categories are listed under the categories.',null)
B.a2K=new A.dA("No subtotal? Add the main category as one of these too, with its items, and each category is added up for you.",null)
B.My=s([B.a2R,B.a2J,B.a2z,B.a2w,B.a2N,B.a2H,B.a2K],t.p)
B.a36=new A.jg("Other categories",B.My,null)
B.a2B=new A.dA("Under the lines, each category shows its amount before tax, its tax and its total, with the whole receipt's total last. Compare that total with the receipt: if they differ, a price was missed or mistyped.",null)
B.LC=s([B.a2B],t.p)
B.a37=new A.jg("Totals",B.LC,null)
B.a2O=new A.dA("Amounts fill from the cents up, like a till: typing 1, 5, 0 gives 1.50. There is no need to type the decimal point. A minus sign makes a refund.",null)
B.Mt=s([B.a2O],t.p)
B.a3a=new A.jg("Typing amounts",B.Mt,null)
B.a2P=new A.dA("Where you shopped, which decides the sales-tax rate. It starts as the store's usual place, or your home. Start typing a city to choose another.",null)
B.M_=s([B.a2P],t.p)
B.a38=new A.jg("Location",B.M_,null)
B.a2D=new A.dA('Save expense shows the receipt as it will be stored, under "Does this match your receipt?". If an amount or the tax differs from the paper, correct it there: the receipt wins.',null)
B.a2I=new A.dA("Save & New files it and clears the form for the next receipt. Save & Home files it and goes back to the home screen. Back returns to the form without saving.",null)
B.a2x=new A.dA("If something would stop the expense from saving, it is said beside the Save expense button while you type.",null)
B.LR=s([B.a2D,B.a2I,B.a2x],t.p)
B.a3c=new A.jg("Saving",B.LR,null)
B.a2M=new A.dA("Everything works without a mouse. Enter moves to the next field in the order a receipt is read: date, store, subtotal, main category, then each other category's letters, item count and items, and finally the note.",null)
B.a2F=new A.dA("Enter in the note moves to Save expense, which shows a ring around it. Press Enter again to save. The check that follows opens with Save & New selected, so one more Enter files the expense and puts you back on the date of a fresh form.",null)
B.a2E=new A.dA("Tab and Shift+Tab move between fields and buttons, including the corrections in the check. Space or Enter presses a selected button. F1 opens this page.",null)
B.a2G=new A.dA("Hold Shift and use the arrow keys to jump to the nearest field in that direction: Shift+Up from the store goes back to the date, and Shift+Down from the subtotal goes to the main category and then the other categories.",null)
B.Nn=s([B.a2M,B.a2F,B.a2E,B.a2G],t.p)
B.a3e=new A.jg("Keyboard",B.Nn,null)
